From 6bef1fbed17734b0c2d2039d20a15241e026045d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman S <429230+has207@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 13:20:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] [XMA] Drain the current frame before ending the XMA work loop

Work() left its decode loop as soon as both input buffers went invalid,
without checking whether the current frame had been fully handed to the
output ring. Consume() transfers at most subframe_decode_count blocks per
pass, so the pass that exhausts the input usually strands the remainder.

Work() clears is_enabled_ on entry and only XMAEnableContext sets it
again, so that leftover PCM can never be delivered, and a game polling
for it never issues the kick that would deliver it.

Fixes NBA Live 06's menu click sfx which deadlocked guest audio thread.
---
 src/xenia/apu/xma_context_new.cc | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/xenia/apu/xma_context_new.cc b/src/xenia/apu/xma_context_new.cc
index d199146d5..57135caa1 100644
--- a/src/xenia/apu/xma_context_new.cc
+++ b/src/xenia/apu/xma_context_new.cc
@@ -186,7 +186,14 @@ bool XmaContextNew::Work() {
     Decode(&data);
     Consume(&output_rb, &data);
 
-    if (!data.IsAnyInputBufferValid() || data.error_status == 4) {
+    // Don't abandon a partially consumed frame. Consume() hands over at most
+    // subframe_decode_count blocks per pass so the pass that exhausts the
+    // input typically leaves the rest of the frame undelivered. Work() has
+    // already cleared is_enabled_ and only XMAEnableContext sets it again.
+    // Game polling for the remainder therefore never kicks and nothing
+    // else can ever deliver it so keep draining until the frame is out.
+    if ((!data.IsAnyInputBufferValid() || data.error_status == 4) &&
+        current_frame_remaining_subframes_ == 0) {
       XELOGAPU(
           "XmaContext {}: Work loop exit - buffers_valid={} error_status={}",
           id(), data.IsAnyInputBufferValid(), data.error_status);
-- 
